    "description": {
      "value": "<p><em>A bill-of-lading book bound in mottled leather, damp-warped but meticulously kept. Every entry is written in the same crabbed cipher — columns of goods, prices, and dates, page after page after page, with a recurring mark that might be a standing stone beside a road. To an untrained eye the rows are noise.</em></p><p><em>The entries simply stop, about half a year ago. Beside the last one, in an irritated, clawed hand, a note in the same cipher — underlined twice.</em></p>",
